      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Each `board_ap_pwoer_action_g3_entry` checks for `AP_PWRSEQ_EVENT_POWER_SHUTDOWN`. That event is only set by `ap_power_force_shutdown()`.\n\nCorrection: it’s the corresponding `board_ap_power_action_g3_run()` that checks `AP_PWRSEQ_EVENT_POWER_SHUTDOWN`, not `board_ap_power_action_g3_entry()`. The `*_g3_entry()` handler is responsible for driving the power signals into the appropriate `G3`-safe state.\n\n\u003e It looks like these 2 error paths (power signals lost and can\u0027t determine CPU state) will no longer trigger a force shutdown.\n\nI will still trigger shutdown, those two error paths still transition the state machine to `AP_POWER_STATE_G3`. Once in `G3`, the sequencing is handled via `ap_pwrseq_start()` when starting the power sequence driver in `AP_POWER_STATE_G3`, which will invoke the board `G3` entry handling as expected.",
